  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-defense art direction, disciplined cyan/red status palette, crisp borders, and clear headline-to-evidence hierarchy. Tablet is the most balanced. Desktop is compositionally uneven: the oversized headline and large empty field overpower a comparatively tiny chain graphic and dense right rail. Mobile remains coherent but becomes cramped, with very small diagram and metadata text. The global header also feels unfinished at smaller widths: labels visibly truncate, the mobile brand name disappears, and “SWIPE →” crowds the navigation.",
    "fix": "Rebalance desktop scale and whitespace by enlarging the evidence visualization or reducing the hero; raise small-text sizes on mobile; and redesign the compact header with a deliberate brand treatment, active-state cue, and cleaner overflow affordance instead of clipped labels.",
